+
+## Restart health bridge
+
+For guarded restart continuation, public `pi.events` supports a synchronous
+`pi-restart-in-dir:ic-health-request` with `{ requestId, sessionId, leafId }`.
+IDs are nonempty strings; `leafId` may also be `null` for an empty session.
+The reply on `pi-restart-in-dir:ic-health-response` is
+`{ requestId, version: 2, ok, sessionId, leafId, error?: string }`, echoing the
+request's correlation fields. A positive reply revalidates the current branch,
+fold ownership and session projection; registered tools alone are not health.
+
+Malformed requests and requests for other sessions on a shared actor bus are
+ignored. A matching session with a stale selected leaf or invalid IC state replies
+with `ok: false` and an error. The listener is disposed at session shutdown and
+registered again on a fresh session start. This bridge never starts a model turn;
+it is not a global startup-turn or extension-readiness gate.
